; Each level's own tuning of the picture, where a player has set none: a line a level,
;   Tune.<level> = exposure, contrast, saturation, warmth
; each a whole number of the options screen's steps, -4 to 4 (a step of exposure is a
; quarter of a stop). A player's own, set with the sliders, are the same lines in
; graphics.chosen and come before these.
;
; The Circle's tower: nothing. It was given half a stop by guess, and the user, with the
; sliders in hand, set it back (2026-10-12: "for mage tower everything 0 looks good to me").
Tune.lak303d = 0, 0, 0, 0
;
; Orzammar's Commons: nothing. It is lit as vanilla lights it again since 2026-10-12 (the user:
; "go back to vanilla lighting. i think what we have is too dark, too extreme. we can then
; slowly tweak it from there"), and the half stop was for its relit bake.
Tune.orz100d = 0, 0, 0, 0
